        "verbatim": true,
        "what": "A cache-cleanup command claude-code constructed for itself. The body passed to sh -c was wrapped in double quotes, so the outer shell expanded the undefined $1 to empty before sh saw it -- what actually ran was rm -rf \"\"/* , i.e. rm -rf /*. It deleted an entire WSL distribution (including a live database) and reached the host's D: drive through /mnt/d. Both were TRIM SSDs, so the data was physically erased. The report names two product defects: no check on the *expanded* result, and the safety classifier refusing the agent's emergency stop twice.",
